- op: discuss  # 27d1
  at: '2026-10-29T09:59:07Z'  # 27d1
  by: agent  # 27d1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 27d1
  clock: 8  # 27d1
  nonce: 27d1  # 27d1
  message: "Fixed in PR #1939 (dev 291a3a2418). STATEMENT RE-SCOPED (was: 'a module analyzed in the importing file's own directory'), because that wording is broader than Python: a library module's directory is never on sys.path, and inside a package there is no implicit relative import. The corpus proved the broad reading wrong -- a first cut applying it to every importer resolved stdlib `import json` in src/poetry (a PEP 420 namespace package) to src/poetry/json/. New statement names the two runs that put a directory below the source root on sys.path: pytest's basedir for a test-tree file, and a directly-run script's own directory. Filed repro re-run on merged dev 291a3a2418 (fixture from the 10-29 premise check): tests/test_a.py `import conftest` -> python:tests/conftest.py:1-1:file:file (was python:conftest:0-0:conftest:external_symbol); the DEPENDENCY linker line drops from 3 to 2 third-party edges (pytest, genuinely third-party; and scripts/run.py `import util`, which has no main guard and so is not a script run directly -- correctly external under the new statement). Tests: test_py_same_directory_import.py through run_behavior_map (conftest, script with main guard, from-import, basedir above a package subdir, submodules each to their file; controls for package, namespace package, library-beside-script, third-party), mutation-checked. Corpus A/B, every changed edge read: libvirt-ci 10 edges external -> in-tree, vmaf 5, poetry 0. Not changed: precedence (Python searches the script dir before the source root; here it is tried after, so no existing resolution moves)."  # 27d1
